      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_140d7a64",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: husband_husband_you_are_my_husband; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a couple dressed in traditional attire, with the text 'husband husband you are my husband' overlaid. The scene is not inherently abusive or hateful, but the repetitive and redundant phrasing of 'husband' in the text may be interpreted as a form of performative or exaggerated affection, potentially intended to be humorous or ironic. However, the text does not contain any direct attacks or harmful stereotypes targeting any protected group. The overall intent appears to be lighthearted or comedic, possibly playing on the idea of over-the-top declarations of marital devotion. There is no evidence of cyberbullying, misogyny, racism, or other forms of toxicity. The meme's intent is likely to evoke amusement through the absurdity of the repeated phrase, rather than to cause harm or promote hate. The visual elements (traditional clothing, smiling couple) do not contribute to harmful content, and the text does not map onto any harmful stereotypes or tropes from the provided knowledge base. The meme is more likely to be a harmless, affectionate joke rather than a harmful or propagandistic message.",
